
Iris Flower Classification Using Multi-Layer Perceptron

About the Project

This project uses a Multi-Layer Perceptron neural network to classify iris flowers into different species based on their flower measurements.

Dataset

The project uses the Iris dataset available in Scikit-learn. It contains 150 flower samples from 3 classes: Setosa, Versicolor, and Virginica.

Each sample has 4 features:
* Sepal length
* Sepal width
* Petal length
* Petal width

What We Do

1. Load the Iris dataset using Scikit-learn.
2. Split the data into training and testing sets using 80:20 and 90:10 ratios.
3. Standardize the input features using StandardScaler.
4. Build an MLP model with two hidden layers containing 10 neurons each.
5. Train the model and make predictions on the test data.
6. Evaluate the model using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1 Score.
7. Display confusion matrices, loss curves, and actual vs predicted graphs.
8. Compare the results of the 80:20 and 90:10 data splits.
